  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Section 56(b)(3), the AMT adjustment for an ISO equals the spread at exercise: ($60 - $25) x 500 shares = $17,500. This amount is added to alternative minimum taxable income in the exercise year, assuming the shares are not sold in the same calendar year. (Sec. 56(b)(3).)
Wrong (A): $0 would apply only if the shares were sold in the same calendar year as exercise, eliminating the AMT adjustment.
Wrong (B): $12,500 equals the exercise price times shares ($25 x 500), which is not how the AMT adjustment is calculated — it is the spread, not the exercise cost.
Wrong (D): $30,000 equals FMV times shares ($60 x 500) and incorrectly omits the subtraction of the exercise price from the calculation.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 907;

-- Q908: Individual Tax Planning: Compensation [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): Under Section 409A(a)(1), a plan violation causes immediate income inclusion of all vested deferrals, plus a 20% additional tax on the amount included, plus an interest charge calculated from the year of deferral. For Mercer''s $300,000, this means $60,000 in additional tax plus compounded interest. (IRC Sec. 409A(a)(1)(B).)
Wrong (A): The 10% early distribution penalty applies to qualified plan distributions under Section 72(t), not to Section 409A violations of nonqualified plans.
Wrong (B): Section 409A violations carry severe penalties; Congress intentionally imposed harsh consequences to enforce compliance with deferral timing rules.
Wrong (C): There is no 50% excise tax under Section 409A; the specific statutory penalty is 20% plus an interest charge on the underpayment.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 908;
